preConditionHook:
// GRIMES'S O%Rng (G08-27, G16-13): the session's OPENING price sits in the top
// `highFraction` of the session's range SO FAR (long), the bottom fraction
// (short). The book's full-session range is knowable only in hindsight, so the
// range TO DATE is used, as the mined candidate itself proposes.
//
// Not SessionOpenNearSessionExtreme, which bands the open against the running
// low in ATRs and reads open-near-low as strength: a different tolerance basis
// AND the opposite polarity, which no negate or flip toggle reaches (merge
// decision 12). Not CloseInTopOfSessionRange (the amended
// CloseNearSessionExtreme), which places the closing price in the same window.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: the twin's date > date[1], mirrored
// as day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)), with the running open/high/low
// held in locals reset on that change. Intraday bars only.
//
// Written MULTIPLIED, never as a ratio, so a session whose high equals its low
// fires both sides rather than raising EL's runtime divide-by-zero. On the
// session's first bar the running extremes are that bar's own, so the test is
// the first bar's own open position in its own range.
//
// Deepest bar touched: 1.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    sessOpen = open[0];
    sessHigh = high[0];
    sessLow = low[0];
} else {
    if (el_gt(high[0], sessHigh)) sessHigh = high[0];
    if (el_lt(low[0], sessLow)) sessLow = low[0];
}
sessBand = highFraction * (sessHigh - sessLow);
